          dealing: 'Eleven rounds. First dealer is chosen at random; the turn to deal passes to the left after each round. In round 1 three cards are dealt to each player, in round 2 four cards, and so on until round 11 when thirteen cards each are dealt. The remainder is placed face down as the stock; the top card is turned face up beside it to start the discard pile. One deck for two players, two decks for three or four.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Form all cards in hand into valid combinations: sets of three or more cards of the same rank, or runs of three or more cards in the same suit in sequence. Aces rank low. Unmatched cards at round end count as penalty points; the player with the lowest total score after eleven rounds wins.',
          gameplay: "The player to dealer's left begins; play is clockwise. Each turn consists of drawing one card (from the top of the stock or the top card of the discard pile; only the top of the discard may be taken) and then discarding one card face up onto the discard pile. A player may go out when, after drawing, they can arrange all but one card into sets and runs, discard that card, and announce they are out; each other player gets one more turn, then the round ends when the turn returns to the player who went out.",
          keyRules: [
            'Eleven rounds with 3 to 13 cards dealt per round; dealer rotates left.',
            'Wild card equals the number of cards dealt that round (round 1 threes wild, round 11 kings wild).',
            'Valid combinations: sets of three or more same rank; runs of three or more same suit in sequence; aces low.',
            "Draw one from stock or top of discard, then discard one. No laying off on other players' melds.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Minimize deadwood by forming sets and runs; use wild cards in combinations where they replace missing cards.',
          intermediate: 'Track which cards have been discarded to infer what opponents need; take from the discard only when it completes or extends a combination.',
          advanced: 'Plan round-by-round: in early rounds with few cards, prioritize flexibility; in later rounds with more cards, optimize for going out before opponents.',
          tips: [
            'Wild cards can form a set by themselves or fill gaps in runs.',
            'Aces are low only; Q-K-A is not a valid run.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
